---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Farooq Q. | Resources"
  description="Curated academic and engineering resources by Farooq Qureshi."
>
  <main>
    <article class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-0 pt-0">
      <div class="space-y-4 mt-0 pt-0">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Calculus
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            <a
              href="https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Paul's Online Math Notes</a
            > is probably the best online resource for Calculus I, II, and III.
          </p>
          <p>
            Thomas' Calculus or Stewart's Calculus for extra practice problems.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a
              href="https://www.science.smith.edu/~callahan/intromine.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Calculus in Context</a
            > is good for seeing calculus applied to real problems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Linear Algebra
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            Yiping Lu's <a
              href="https://2prime.github.io/files/linear/midterm_review.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Linear Algebra Cheat Sheet</a
            > is a great review sheet for matrix operations and transformations.
          </p>
          <p>
            MiniReference's <a
              href="https://minireference.com/static/tutorials/linear_algebra_in_4_pages.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Linear Algebra in 4 Pages</a
            > summarizes the key formulas on a few pages.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Differential Equations
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            Jiří Lebl's <a
              href="https://www.jirka.org/diffyqs/diffyqs.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Notes on Diffy Qs</a
            > is a solid free textbook for differential equations.
          </p>
          <p>
            UNCW's <a
              href="https://people.uncw.edu/hermanr/mat361/ODEsheet.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">ODE Reference Sheet</a
            > is handy for quick formula lookups.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Circuits
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            The <a
              href="https://www.falstad.com/circuit/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Falstad Circuit Simulator</a
            > lets you build and visualize circuits directly in your browser.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a
              href="https://www.allaboutcircuits.com/textbook/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">All About Circuits</a
            > has clear explanations for circuit theory and analysis.
          </p>
          <p>
            MIT's <a
              href="https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-002-circuits-and-electronics-spring-2007/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Circuits and Electronics (6.002)</a
            > has good problem sets and lab materials.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sanfoundry’s <a
              href="https://www.sanfoundry.com/electrical-engineering-questions-answers/#1st-year-electrical-engineering-mcq"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">50,000+ Electrical Engineering MCQs</a
            > is a massive bank of practice questions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Electronics
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            Behzad Razavi’s <a
              href="https://www.youtube.com/@b_razavi/featured"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">YouTube channel</a
            > is amazing for learning microelectronics and circuit design.
          </p>
          <p>
            Analog Devices’ <a
              href="https://wiki.analog.com/university/courses/electronics"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Electronics Course wiki</a
            > has great practical lab materials and circuit design notes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-medium opacity-60 m-0 p-0">
          Electromagnetics
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p>
            The <a
              href="https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/II_toc.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Feynman Lectures on Physics (Vol. II)</a
            > is great for building real intuition for electromagnetism and Maxwell's equations.
          </p>
          <p>
            David Tong's <a
              href="https://davidtong.org/teaching/electromagnetism/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Electromagnetism lecture notes</a
            > from Cambridge are fantastic.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
